# Git Workflow

## Branch Strategy

- `main` - Production-ready code, protected
- `develop` - Integration branch for features
- `feature/*` - New features (e.g., `feature/video-call-room`)
- `fix/*` - Bug fixes (e.g., `fix/stripe-webhook-timeout`)
- `chore/*` - Tooling, deps, config (e.g., `chore/upgrade-turbo`)

## Commit Conventions

Follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/):

```
feat(api): add consultation booking endpoint
fix(mobile): resolve date picker timezone issue
chore(deps): upgrade Stripe SDK to v17
docs(readme): update setup instructions
refactor(shared): extract user types to separate file
test(api): add webhook handler tests
```

## Pull Requests

- PRs require at least one review before merging
- Keep PRs focused and small (< 500 lines when possible)
- Include testing instructions and screenshots for UI changes
- Link related issues in the description

## Before Committing

1. Run `pnpm lint` to check code quality
2. Run `pnpm typecheck` to verify TypeScript
3. Run relevant tests: `pnpm test`
4. Ensure no `.env` files are staged
5. Use `git add -p` for granular staging

## Never Commit

- `.env` files or any files containing secrets
- `node_modules/` (gitignored)
- Build outputs: `.next/`, `dist/`, `.expo/`
- `.turbo/` cache
- IDE-specific settings (except shared `.vscode/settings.json`)
